[%# This exists for the outbound half.  setup-ufw-rules issues "allow out" for
    every profile in /etc/ufw/applications.d, and the guests this builds default
    to deny outgoing -- so without a profile naming the destination port, rsyslog
    cannot open a connection to the collector at all, and says nothing about it.

    It opens the port inbound as well, which is what that script does for every
    profile.  Nothing is listening on it here: a shipper loads no input module,
    so the inbound half reaches a closed port.

    Not named syslog, because ufw skips a profile whose section name is also a
    service name in /etc/services and only warns about it on stderr. -%]
[logshipper]
title=Log shipper
description=Outbound syslog to the collector this guest was configured with
ports=[% port %]/[% protocol %]
